-- title:
--   Kernel of R_Q→ R_{min} generated by diamonds minus one (flat case)
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation ring (a domain, a discrete valuation ring, adically complete for its maximal ideal), let $p$ be a natural number and let $S_{\min}, Q$ be finite sets of natural numbers such that every $q\in Q$ is prime and does not lie in $S_{\min}$. Fix a residual representation $\bar\rho$ over the residue field of $\mathcal O$: a two-dimensional space with a Galois action of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ factoring through a finite level. Let $D_{\min}$ be a deformation ring datum for $\bar\rho$ with the minimal flat condition of type $S_{\min}$ (cyclotomic determinant, flat at $p$, unramified at every prime outside $S_{\min}$, and charpoly $(X-1)^2$ on inertia at every prime $q\in S_{\min}$ with $q\neq p$), and let $D_Q$ be one for the condition relaxed at $Q$ (the same flat condition with $S_{\min}\cup Q$ in place of $S_{\min}$, together with unipotence on inertia at the primes of $S_{\min}$ different from $p$); each datum carries its universal ring $R$, its deformation $\rho$ of $\bar\rho$ and the universal property. Let $\varepsilon\colon R_Q\to R_{\min}$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra map which is a local homomorphism and along which the base change of $\rho_Q$ is equivalent to $\rho_{\min}$. Let $k\colon\mathbb N\to\mathbb N$; for each $q$ let $\mathrm{cyc}_q\colon \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)\to(\mathbb Z/q)^{\times}$ be a homomorphism which for $q\in Q$ describes the Galois action on $q$-th roots of unity ($\sigma\mu=\mu^{\mathrm{cyc}_q(\sigma)}$ whenever $\mu^q=1$), let $\pi_{\Delta,q}\colon(\mathbb Z/q)^{\times}\to\mathbb Z/p^{k(q)}$ (multiplicative) be homomorphisms, surjective for $q\in Q$, and let $\chi_q\colon\mathbb Z/p^{k(q)}\to R_Q^{\times}$ be homomorphisms such that for $q\in Q$ and every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $P$ there is an $R_Q$-basis $b_0,b_1$ of the underlying module of $\rho_Q$ on which every element $\sigma$ of the inertia subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb Q$ acts by $\chi_q(\pi_{\Delta,q}(\mathrm{cyc}_q(\sigma)))$ and its inverse respectively. Finally let $\iota\colon\mathcal O[\prod_{q\in Q}\mathbb Z/p^{k(q)}]\to R_Q$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra map sending a group element $g$ to $\prod_{q\in Q}\chi_q(g_q)$. Then the kernel of $\varepsilon$ is the ideal of $R_Q$ generated by the elements $\iota(g)-1$ as $g$ ranges over $\prod_{q\in Q}\mathbb Z/p^{k(q)}$.
--
--   This is the flat analogue of the Taylor–Wiles description of the relaxation map between the deformation ring of Taylor–Wiles level $Q$ and the minimal one: the augmentation ideal of the diamond group $\Delta_Q=\prod_{q\in Q}\mathbb Z/p^{k(q)}$, pushed into $R_Q$ by the diamond-operator map $\iota$, cuts out $R_{\min}$. It is used in the assembly of the patching data for the Hecke-algebra side of the modularity lifting argument.
